WEBVTT

00:01.120 --> 00:02.440
Today,  more  and  more  people  are

00:02.440 --> 00:03.520
turning  to  AI  to  build

00:03.520 --> 00:05.720
personalized  workout  programs.

00:05.720 --> 00:07.120
And  AI  is  actually  really  good  at

00:07.120 --> 00:08.280
it.  You  can  tell  your  fitness

00:08.280 --> 00:09.440
goals,  how  many  days  you  want  to

00:09.440 --> 00:11.519
work  out,  any  injuries  you  have

00:11.519 --> 00:12.840
and  what  equipment  you  have  access

00:12.840 --> 00:14.879
to  to  get  a  completely  customized

00:14.879 --> 00:17.119
program  within  seconds.

00:17.119 --> 00:19.080
But  there's  a  problem.  Once  AI

00:19.080 --> 00:20.960
creates  that  program,  what  do  you

00:20.960 --> 00:22.600
actually  do  with  it?

00:22.600 --> 00:23.920
Today,  you're  either  copying

00:23.920 --> 00:26.080
exercises  from  your  AI  tool  into

00:26.080 --> 00:27.679
another  workout  app  or  maybe

00:27.679 --> 00:29.880
manually  building  out  a  spreadsheet

00:29.880 --> 00:31.240
or  or  even  having  everything  in  a

00:31.240 --> 00:33.000
conversation  directly  with  your  AI

00:33.000 --> 00:34.040
tool.

00:34.040 --> 00:35.440
There's  a  real  disconnect  between

00:35.440 --> 00:37.280
creating  that  workout  and  actually

00:37.280 --> 00:39.800
putting  the  workout  into  action.

00:39.800 --> 00:41.160
And  that's  exactly  why  I  built

00:41.160 --> 00:42.079
Buff.

00:42.079 --> 00:43.920
Buff  bridges  the  gap  by  combining

00:43.920 --> 00:46.440
AI  powered  workout  program  creation

00:46.440 --> 00:47.920
with  a  simple  intuitive  workout

00:47.920 --> 00:50.039
tracking  experience  all  in  one

00:50.039 --> 00:51.160
place.

00:51.160 --> 00:52.740
Let  me  show  you  how  it  works.

00:54.087 --> 00:55.767
Let's start by introducing you to our

00:55.767 --> 00:57.607
built-in AI coach Buffy.

00:58.287 --> 00:59.927
Creating a workout program from scratch

00:59.927 --> 01:01.447
can be overwhelming. You have to figure

01:01.447 --> 01:03.087
out which exercises to include,

01:03.367 --> 01:04.927
how to split up muscle groups and how

01:04.927 --> 01:06.167
many sets and reps to do.

01:06.807 --> 01:08.727
With Buffy, you don't have to figure all

01:08.727 --> 01:09.807
of that out yourself.

01:10.407 --> 01:12.247
Instead, you can have a conversation with

01:12.247 --> 01:15.047
Buffy using natural language to create a

01:15.047 --> 01:17.367
program that focuses on your goals.

01:18.127 --> 01:20.047
And Buffy doesn't just take your first

01:20.047 --> 01:21.407
request and run with it.

01:21.847 --> 01:24.207
Instead, it asks thoughtful questions,

01:24.447 --> 01:26.487
making sure it has all the information it

01:26.487 --> 01:28.327
needs to give you the best program

01:28.327 --> 01:28.807
possible.

01:31.743 --> 01:33.463
Within  moments,  Buffy  returns  a

01:33.463 --> 01:35.463
structured  workout  program.  It

01:35.463 --> 01:36.383
gives  me  a  breakdown  of  my

01:36.383 --> 01:37.862
program,  showing  me  my  weekly

01:37.862 --> 01:40.223
exercises  and  goals.  And  once  I've

01:40.223 --> 01:41.623
reviewed  the  program,  I  can  ask

01:41.623 --> 01:44.102
Buffy  to  make  changes.  Or  I  can

01:44.102 --> 01:45.783
save  it  directly  to  my  program

01:45.783 --> 01:47.023
library.

01:47.023 --> 01:48.383
No  more  copy  and  pasting  workouts

01:48.383 --> 01:49.902
from  an  AI  tool  into  a  workout

01:49.902 --> 01:51.902
app.  With  Buff,  I  have  everything

01:51.902 --> 01:54.523
in  one  place.

01:55.022 --> 01:56.782
Now that I've created my program, let's

01:56.782 --> 01:58.062
head back to the home screen.

01:58.782 --> 02:00.502
One thing I really wanted Buff to do was

02:00.502 --> 02:02.782
eliminate the question of what workout am

02:02.782 --> 02:03.702
I supposed to do today.

02:04.422 --> 02:06.062
That's why Buff automatically highlights

02:06.062 --> 02:07.902
my upcoming workout right here.

02:08.542 --> 02:09.982
I don't have to dig through my programs

02:09.982 --> 02:11.622
or try to remember where I left off.

02:11.902 --> 02:13.662
I can open the app, immediately see

02:13.662 --> 02:15.342
what's next and jump straight into my

02:15.342 --> 02:15.942
workout.

02:16.582 --> 02:18.542
It's a small detail, but we all know that

02:18.542 --> 02:20.222
starting your workout is the hardest part

02:20.582 --> 02:22.662
and we want to remove any barriers to

02:22.662 --> 02:23.222
getting there.

02:23.982 --> 02:24.462
I think I can see

02:25.062 --> 02:25.142
that.

02:26.434 --> 02:28.114
Now let's get into the workout itself.

02:28.354 --> 02:30.194
When I open a workout, I can see all of

02:30.194 --> 02:32.354
my exercises along with my target sets

02:32.354 --> 02:32.914
and reps.

02:33.554 --> 02:34.794
But here's what I really love.

02:35.074 --> 02:37.154
Buff also keeps track of my previous

02:37.154 --> 02:39.354
performance. So I can see exactly what I

02:39.354 --> 02:41.154
lifted the last time I completed each

02:41.154 --> 02:41.954
exercise.

02:42.514 --> 02:43.954
Instead of trying to remember what weight

02:43.954 --> 02:46.114
I used or how many reps I completed, that

02:46.114 --> 02:47.594
information is right here.

02:48.394 --> 02:50.354
This makes it easy to challenge myself,

02:50.514 --> 02:52.634
track my progress over time and focus on

02:52.634 --> 02:53.634
getting stronger.

02:54.567 --> 02:56.327
Let's have a focusing on squats today.

02:56.607 --> 02:58.527
I can see that I previously lifted 95

02:58.527 --> 02:59.687
pounds for 10 reps.

03:00.247 --> 03:02.127
I can use this as my starting point for

03:02.127 --> 03:03.047
today's workout.

03:04.007 --> 03:06.047
Once I complete my set, I populate my

03:06.047 --> 03:07.247
weight and reps

03:07.727 --> 03:09.367
and mark the sets as complete.

03:10.327 --> 03:12.607
And because logging each set is quick and

03:12.607 --> 03:13.287
intuitive,

03:13.647 --> 03:15.767
I can spend less time on my phone and

03:15.767 --> 03:18.167
more time actually working out.

03:19.776 --> 03:21.256
Now, let's say I'm halfway through my

03:21.256 --> 03:22.696
workout and the equipment need is being

03:22.696 --> 03:25.056
used or I just want to switch things up.

03:25.456 --> 03:27.816
With buff, I can easily swap an exercise

03:27.816 --> 03:29.376
without having to change my entire

03:29.376 --> 03:29.936
workout.

03:30.576 --> 03:32.496
Maybe I want to replace split squats with

03:32.496 --> 03:33.496
a different exercise.

03:33.936 --> 03:35.896
I can simply select the option to swap

03:35.936 --> 03:38.456
and search buff's extensive exercise

03:38.456 --> 03:40.056
library for an alternative.

03:40.736 --> 03:42.376
When I search for lunges, it brings up

03:42.376 --> 03:43.896
several variations.

03:44.416 --> 03:46.456
I can review the exercise instructions

03:46.456 --> 03:48.656
before selecting the new exercise and

03:48.696 --> 03:49.856
saving it to my workout.

03:51.256 --> 03:53.376
The idea is simple. Your workout should

03:53.376 --> 03:54.336
adapt to you,

03:54.656 --> 03:55.936
not the other way around.

03:56.576 --> 03:58.096
Our AI coach, Buffy,

03:58.376 --> 03:59.976
builds you a program to help you set a

03:59.976 --> 04:01.216
strong foundation

04:01.616 --> 04:03.456
and using the Buff app gives you the

04:03.456 --> 04:05.536
flexibility to make changes as you go.

04:07.208 --> 04:09.048
Once I'm finished, I can mark my workout

04:09.048 --> 04:11.368
as complete, which creates a record of

04:11.368 --> 04:12.528
what I've accomplished.

04:12.848 --> 04:14.888
The next time I come back to the gym, I'm

04:14.888 --> 04:16.648
not trying to remember how much I lifted

04:16.648 --> 04:18.128
or how many reps I completed.

04:18.568 --> 04:21.368
I can look back at my previous workouts

04:21.408 --> 04:23.128
and use that information to keep

04:23.128 --> 04:24.168
challenging myself.

04:24.728 --> 04:26.208
For me, that's what makes workout

04:26.208 --> 04:27.328
tracking so valuable.

04:27.648 --> 04:29.728
It's not just about checking a box today.

04:29.968 --> 04:31.688
It's about being able to look back and

04:31.688 --> 04:32.848
see how far you've come.
